  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 128 PM MDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nNo impacts related to the weather through Wednesday as clear\nskies continue. After the very cool conditions Tuesday expect\ntemperatures back near seasonal normal on Wednesday and then\nwell above normal Thursday as a much stronger zonal westerly\nflow aloft moves into Idaho. Many low elevation high\ntemperatures back to around 80 degrees on Wednesday then mid to\neven upper 80s by Thursday. Mountains likely well into the 70s\nmost locations on Thursday as well. Winds in the 10 to 20 mph\nrange Thursday then in the 15 to 30 mph range on Friday mainly\nin the Snake River Plain and Arco Desert. Models indicating a\nchance of an upper level low pressure and strong cold front\nmoving through next Sunday increasing a chance of showers and\nthunderstorms mainly in the mountains but mainly another\nsignificant cool down Sunday into next Monday before warming\ncommences again. Upcoming seasonal change being indicated as\neach cold front brings even cooler conditions than the previous\none. Overall not expecting significant rainfall through the next\nweek.",
